  "notes": "USAGE:\nTakes the particle に to mark what one is soaking in: ～に{浸|つ}かる. The most common usage is お{風呂|ふろ}に{浸|つ}かる (to soak in the bath).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{浸|ひた}る also means \"to be immersed\" but is more literary and tends to emphasize the figurative sense of being absorbed in something. {浸|つ}かる is more common for physical soaking.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- お{風呂|ふろ}に{浸|つ}かる: to soak in the bath\n- {温泉|おんせん}に{浸|つ}かる: to soak in a hot spring\n- {水|みず}に{浸|つ}かる: to be submerged in water\n- {余韻|よいん}に{浸|つ}かる: to bask in the afterglow\n- {思|おも}い{出|で}に{浸|つ}かる: to be lost in memories",
